##
## Slab phase-separation demo parameter file.
##
## A single "sticky" bead type S with a strong self-attraction, so that a dense,
## high-concentration melt of S-polymers demixes from solvent (empty sites) into a
## condensed phase in coexistence with a dilute vapour.
##
## Bead types:  S = sticky monomer
##

## ANGLE PENALTIES (must be defined for every bead type, even if zero)
## Fully flexible chains - no backbone stiffness.
ANGLE_PENALTY	S	0	0	0

## PAIRWISE INTERACTIONS
## A single strongly-attractive short-range contact energy drives condensation.
## (Same energy scale as the two_phase_equilibrium_demo, which phase-separates at
## a comparable temperature.)
S	S	-20

## bead-solvent interactions (the "<type> 0 <energy>" line). Zero here, so the only
## thermodynamic driving force is the S-S self-attraction above.
S	0	0
